From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Kamil=20Postro=C5=BCny?= <kamil@postrozny.pl>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:07:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: query placed-memory properties through the KHR entry
 point

D3DKMT creates a Vulkan 1.0 instance with
VK_KHR_get_physical_device_properties2. On a WoW64 process with
VK_EXT_map_memory_placed the Features2KHR call succeeds, but the
following core Properties2 call is NULL on KosmicKrisp. Use the KHR
entry point consistently, as the external-memory-host query already
does. Tomb Raider reaches this during its D3D11 adapter probe.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-09-tomb-raider-memory-read.md
Offered-upstream: no; not yet submitted
---
 dlls/win32u/vulkan.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
index 48524c5..1abf706 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -537,7 +537,9 @@ static VkResult init_physical_device( struct vulkan_physical_device *physical_de
             VkPhysicalDeviceMapMemoryPlacedPropertiesEXT map_placed_props = {.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_MAP_MEMORY_PLACED_PROPERTIES_EXT};
             VkPhysicalDeviceProperties2 props = {.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_PROPERTIES_2,.pNext = &map_placed_props};
 
-            instance->p_vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2( host_physical_device, &props );
+            /* Like the Features2 query above, use the enabled KHR entry point:
+             * D3DKMT's Vulkan 1.0 instance has no core 1.1 Properties2 pointer. */
+            instance->p_vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2KHR( host_physical_device, &props );
             physical_device->map_placed_align = map_placed_props.minPlacedMemoryMapAlignment;
             TRACE( "Using placed map with alignment %u\n", physical_device->map_placed_align );
         }
